{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "ddd9f388-ac70-4ef5-ad14-ead618f3814c"/*FaceDetectionExample*/,
  "Description": "Detects faces in a live camera image and shows the built-in debug view: the camera frame with a bounding box, its confidence score and the 6 facial keypoints per face.\n\nThe example's output is that debug view, so it needs [Debug] on - with [Debug] off it goes blank, and the clean camera image is then only available on the operator's [OutputTexture] output. The detections are provided as data: [PointBuffer] holds 4 corner points per detected face in image space (X from -aspect to aspect, Y from -1 to 1, Y down like screen space), with F1 encoding the corner index (faceIndex * 10 + corner) and F2 the detection confidence. [FaceCount] holds the number of faces.\n\nThis is the lightweight blazeface-style detector - use it for presence, tracking and framing; use [FaceLandmarkDetectionExample] when the detailed face mesh is needed.",
  "InputUis": [],
  "SymbolChildUis": [
