  "Sections": [
    {
      "Id": "4bf824b1-51e4-48d9-83c5-79c0e8e4fbd1",
      "Title": "This example needs a camera\n\n1. Select the [VideoDeviceInput] op\n2. Pick the camera in the InputDeviceName field\n3. Tick [Active] - put yourself (or a hand / objects) in view\n\nThe output shows the operator's debug view with the detected landmarks - keep its [Debug] input on, or the view goes blank. The clean camera image is on the operator's [OutputTexture] output, and the detections (PointBuffer, counts, ...) are available as data to drive your own visuals.",
      "Label": "Setup your camera",
      "Color": {
